WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.095
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.395 --> 00:00:08.677
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.977 --> 00:00:14.392
Unit twenty-one: On the Phone. In this unit, you will make and answer a polite phone call.

4
00:00:15.383 --> 00:00:16.419
Phone call.

5
00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:19.873
Phone call means talking to someone using a phone.

6
00:00:20.173 --> 00:00:21.952
I got a phone call from my aunt.

7
00:00:22.652 --> 00:00:25.351
Your turn. Say: Phone call.

8
00:00:28.051 --> 00:00:29.052
Phone call.

9
00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:30.981
Hello.

10
00:00:31.681 --> 00:00:34.157
Hello means what you say when you answer the phone.

11
00:00:34.457 --> 00:00:36.503
Hello, this is Sreypich.

12
00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:40.006
Your turn. Say: Hello.

13
00:00:42.706 --> 00:00:43.510
Hello.

14
00:00:44.517 --> 00:00:45.506
Speak to.

15
00:00:46.206 --> 00:00:47.927
Speak to means talk with a person.

16
00:00:48.227 --> 00:00:49.716
Could I speak to your mother?

17
00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:53.126
Your turn. Say: Speak to.

18
00:00:55.826 --> 00:00:56.885
Speak to.

19
00:00:57.883 --> 00:00:58.873
Message.

20
00:00:59.573 --> 00:01:02.675
Message means information you give to someone who isn't there.

21
00:01:02.975 --> 00:01:04.278
Can I take a message?

22
00:01:04.978 --> 00:01:07.375
Your turn. Say: Message.

23
00:01:10.075 --> 00:01:10.983
Message.

24
00:01:11.983 --> 00:01:12.857
Call back.

25
00:01:13.557 --> 00:01:15.939
Call back means to phone someone again later.

26
00:01:16.239 --> 00:01:17.566
Please call me back.

27
00:01:18.266 --> 00:01:21.034
Your turn. Say: Call back.

28
00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:24.758
Call back.

29
00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:26.739
Hold on.

30
00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:29.462
Hold on means wait a moment on the phone.

31
00:01:29.762 --> 00:01:30.879
Hold on, please.

32
00:01:31.579 --> 00:01:34.464
Your turn. Say: Hold on.

33
00:01:37.164 --> 00:01:38.153
Hold on.

34
00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:40.012
Number.

35
00:01:40.712 --> 00:01:43.118
Number means the digits you use to call someone.

36
00:01:43.418 --> 00:01:44.744
What's your phone number?

37
00:01:45.444 --> 00:01:48.410
Your turn. Say: Number.

38
00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:51.948
Number.

39
00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:53.823
Goodbye.

40
00:01:54.523 --> 00:01:56.848
Goodbye means what you say at the end of a call.

41
00:01:57.148 --> 00:01:58.964
Thank you. Goodbye!

42
00:01:59.664 --> 00:02:02.027
Your turn. Say: Goodbye.

43
00:02:04.727 --> 00:02:05.565
Goodbye.

44
00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:08.782
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:09.082 --> 00:02:11.859
Hello, could I speak to Mr. Sok, please?

46
00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:16.218
Hold on, please... I'm sorry, he isn't here.

47
00:02:17.517 --> 00:02:19.948
Oh. Could you ask him to call me back?

48
00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.659
Of course. Can I take your number?

49
00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:30.015
Yes, it's 012 345 678.

50
00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:34.599
Thank you. I'll give him the message. Goodbye!

51
00:02:35.883 --> 00:02:40.068
Grammar focus: Could I speak to ? and Can I take a message?.

52
00:02:40.368 --> 00:02:42.345
Could I speak to Dara, please?

53
00:02:42.645 --> 00:02:47.027
On the phone, say your name: 'Hello, this is Sreypich.' Then ask politely.

54
00:02:48.017 --> 00:02:50.634
Now read and listen. A Polite Phone Call.

55
00:02:50.934 --> 00:02:52.910
Yesterday, I phoned my friend Dara.

56
00:02:54.217 --> 00:02:58.819
His sister answered, and I said, “Hello, could I speak to Dara, please?”

57
00:03:00.117 --> 00:03:05.294
She said, “Hold on, please. Sorry, he isn't here. Can I take a message?”

58
00:03:06.583 --> 00:03:09.860
I asked her to tell Dara to call me back and gave my number.

59
00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:13.126
In the evening, Dara called me back.

60
00:03:14.417 --> 00:03:17.208
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:17.508 --> 00:03:19.415
Could I blank to Dara, please?

62
00:03:19.715 --> 00:03:23.508
A, speak. B, speaks. C, speaking.

63
00:03:27.517 --> 00:03:29.435
The answer is A: speak.

64
00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.984
'Wait a moment' on the phone is blank.

65
00:03:33.284 --> 00:03:36.706
A, hold on. B, goodbye. C, call back.

66
00:03:40.717 --> 00:03:42.716
The answer is A: hold on.

67
00:03:44.217 --> 00:03:45.462
Can I take a blank?

68
00:03:45.762 --> 00:03:48.997
A, message. B, number. C, hello.

69
00:03:52.983 --> 00:03:55.331
The answer is A: message.

70
00:03:56.817 --> 00:04:00.537
Now it's your turn to speak. How do you start a polite phone call?

71
00:04:05.837 --> 00:04:11.084
I say, “Hello, this is Sreypich. Could I speak to Mrs. Lina, please?”

72
00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:13.290
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:14.283 --> 00:04:19.469
Great work today! You learned eight new words and could i speak to ? and can i take a message?.

74
00:04:19.769 --> 00:04:24.128
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

75
00:04:24.428 --> 00:04:27.127
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

76
00:04:27.427 --> 00:04:30.416
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

